        "mission_intent": "We need a complete System Transition Security Specification for the upcoming deployment of our next-generation Maritime Domain Awareness platform (MDA-X) from the integration lab into the operational environment at three coastal watch centers. This specification should be aligned with the NIST SP 800-160 Volume 1 guidance on the Transition process and must address how we establish the capability for MDA-X to deliver services as defined by our stakeholder requirements baseline while maintaining full security posture throughout. Specifically, the document must cover confidentiality protections for all transition activities, methods, materiel, tooling, and personnel information involved in system assembly, checkout, and commissioning at each site. It needs to define interim secure storage requirements for all system elements during transit and staging, establish chain-of-custody and accountability procedures for every deliverable component throughout the transition lifecycle, and specify security qualification and authorization criteria for all personnel participating in installation, integration, and handover activities. Critically, the spec must include integrity verification procedures ensuring that the system as delivered and installed at each watch center corresponds precisely to the validated configuration from our integration lab baseline. Please reference ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288:2015 process definitions where applicable and ensure traceability to our existing stakeholder requirements. We need a draft ready for engineering review by the end of next month so we can support the first site's transition window in Q3.",
